Q 3. Create a configuration file to launch in a Kubernetes cluster with the following instructions:  	     [10 Marks]

1. Pull the PHP with Apache image
2. It should launch 5 pods for the above image
3. The container name should be provided
4. The container port should be 80 which is mapped to port 8080 on the localhost
5. Create a deployment once the configuration file is done.


kubectl create deployment php-apache-deployment \
  --image=php:apache \
  --replicas=5


kubectl expose deployment php-apache-deployment \
  --name=php-apache-service \
  --port=8080 \
  --target-port=80 \
  --type=NodePort

kubectl get pods

kubectl get svc


